.333, "branches": 3, "notes": "Watkins ch. 43: Germanic 'become the bane' (ON at bana verða, OE tō banan weorðan) as the periphrastic continuant of *gʷʰen-, with the agent noun *gʷʰonós = Ved. ghaná- 'striker'; Vedic has the same construction, 'you became the striker of the vṛtras' (RV 1.4.8, cf. 8.96.18). Grípisspá 11: Sigurðr will slay the serpent Fáfnir. 'Become' is *bʰuH- with the Vedic (Gmc. verða is *wert-, Gk. γένοντο *ǵenh₁-), so not secure. Greek φόνος is the action noun (lexeme gʷʰónos-2), not this agent noun. 'Serpent' is interpolated (Ved. vṛtrá-, ON ormr < *wr̥mis)."}
